## Root cause

`send_with_retry()` leaked a packet buffer on every failed send.

- Each attempt called `encode_frame()` → `malloc(len + 8)` (4104 bytes).
- Per `link.h`, `link_send()` only takes ownership on `ESP_OK`; on error **the caller keeps ownership** and must free it.
- On error the code just looped, overwrote `pkt.data` with the next allocation, and never freed the previous one. When all attempts failed it also dropped the last buffer.
- The simulated radio returns `ESP_ERR_TIMEOUT` on roughly every 5th call, so ~10–12 leaks/second × ~4 KB ≈ 50 KB/s.
- `CONFIG_SPIRAM` is **not** enabled in `sdkconfig`, so `malloc` comes from internal SRAM (~390 KB free). Within a few seconds the heap was exhausted, `encode_frame()` (and eventually `build_frame()`) failed, and every send failed.

## Fix (`main/main.c`)

Encode **once**, retry `link_send()` with the same packet (legal, since the caller retains ownership on error), and free the buffer if no attempt is accepted:

```c
static esp_err_t send_with_retry(const uint8_t *frame, size_t len)
{
    link_packet_t pkt;
    pkt.data = encode_frame(frame, len, &pkt.len);
    if (pkt.data == NULL) {
        return ESP_ERR_NO_MEM;
    }
    for (int attempt = 0; attempt < MAX_ATTEMPTS; attempt++) {
        esp_err_t err = link_send(&pkt);
        if (err == ESP_OK) {
            return ESP_OK;          /* link now owns pkt.data */
        }
        ESP_LOGW(TAG, "send failed (%s), retrying", esp_err_to_name(err));
        retries++;
    }
    free(pkt.data);                 /* never handed off */
    return ESP_FAIL;
}
```

No changes to `link.c`/`link.h`, frame size, or the 50 Hz rate.

## Verification on the board

Flashed `/dev/cu.usbmodem101` and monitored for 40 s. `heap_free` is now constant at **391916** (was draining before), `failed=0`, and `sent` climbs continuously:

```
stats seq=1250 sent=1251 retries=312 failed=0 queue=0 heap_free=391916
stats seq=2100 sent=2101 retries=525 failed=0 queue=0 heap_free=391916
```

Sends continue indefinitely with the expected occasional `ESP_ERR_TIMEOUT` retries (radio busy), but no memory growth.
